Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(geometry): the edge-parity duplicate drop runs only
 in weld_at_f32; weld keeps its first copy (#4182 review)

Review of #4237 (finding 1): `repair::weld` is also what RepairModel runs
on a part model, and the parity rule removed double-sided surfaces there
(a double-sided sheet to nothing, a double-sided fin off a cube).

- `drop_degenerate` takes a `Duplicates` rule. `weld` keeps the first
  copy of every duplicate set, as on main; `weld_at_f32`, whose input is
  a closed surface, settles duplicates by edge parity.
- `weld_at_f32` also welds when two distinct corners meet at f32 without
  a collapse (review's optional item), and `file_bytes` checks that mesh.
- Pins: `a_double_sided_sheet_keeps_its_facets_through_repair` and
  `a_double_sided_fin_on_a_cube_stays_through_repair` (RepairModel);
  `two_solids_whose_edges_meet_in_the_file_are_refused` and
  `a_sliver_that_collapses_to_nothing_as_written_is_refused` (export);
  the back-to-back pin now goes through `weld_at_f32`.
- Decision file updated; corner gaps in comments are nm, not um.

